likelier: a guild or craft council in the county, an old master who pushes, a workshop of one's own, years of pieces sold
rarer: no guild within reach, a maker who sells well without a mark, hands or eyes beginning to fail
gap: 2-4
domain: career.5
tone: mixed
life: work, community
horizon: months
roles: mentor, grandparent, colleague, rival, friend
earth: the makers' guild judges masterpieces for its mark once a year, in the old hall
tribal: the master carvers of the gathering judge a new carver's piece, to cut the band's sign beside the maker's own
magic: the craft guild's masters sit to judge a journeyman's masterpiece for the guild's mark
scene: Once a year the county's makers' guild judges pieces for its mark in the old corn exchange: three masters, a long table, a magnifying glass, and no talking. {N} has been a maker for years, and {mentor} says this is the year.
scene W: The guild's standard is written down to the last joint and glaze, and {N} has a copy pinned above the bench. Every line of it is a promise to whoever will use the piece.
scene U: {N} has been working on one problem for two winters: a joint that holds without glue or pin. If it works, the masters will not have seen it before.
scene B: The guild's mark doubles the price of a piece overnight. {N} knows which shops in the city stock only marked work.
scene R: {N} has dreamed of one piece for ten years and never had the nerve. The guild's day is a reason to make it at last.
scene G: The wood is from the old ash that fell in the storm behind the house of {grandparent}, seasoned six years in the shed. {N} knows its grain like a face.
scene tribal: At the gathering the master carvers sit in a row on the hides, and any carver who thinks the work is ready lays one piece before them. If they nod, the band's sign is cut beside the maker's own.
scene magic: The craft guild's masters sit in their hall once a year to judge the journeymen's masterpieces. A piece that passes earns the guild's mark, the right to keep an apprentice, and a seat at the guild's table.
